m. Drop the question mark: **\"Good afternoon!\"** It needs no doubt.\n\nNow the question about \"Good morning\". Let's go one tiny step at a time.\n\nLook at a clock. The day has three parts:\n- **morning:** before 12 p.m.\n- **afternoon:** 12 p.m. to about 6 p.m.\n- **evening:** after about 6 p.m.\n\nEach greeting matches one part, like lunch matches the middle of the day.\n\n**One small question:** Is 3 p.m. **before** 12 p.m. or **after** 12 p.m.?","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-001","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-001","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["corrective_feedback_retry","comprehensible_model"],"reasonCodes":["answer_to_instruction","level_novice_prompt_first","recurrence_unknown","after_confirmed_success","level_beginner","during_feedback"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"learner_retry","provenance":"deterministic_turn_signals","confidence":"low","masteryClaim":false,"policyRevision":"ltc-v1-r4.3","pendingTask":"instruction","learnerResponse":"answer","learnerIntent":"PARTIAL_ANSWER_ATTEMPT","stateScope":"3102a06eec317ebdb1c4288a","attemptsOnTask":3,"lengthTarget":{"targetWords":90,"maxWords":140,"basis":"adult:a2"},"errorRecurrence":"unknown","ageBand":"adult","ageBandStatus":"known","ageBandSource":"school_setting_adult_learners","confirmedSuccessStreak":1,"hintLevelOffered":1,"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569515715-i9um","source":"tutor"},"assessment":{"verdict":"PARTIALLY_CORRECT","relevance":"ACTIVE_ITEM","criteria":[],"next":"NEW_ITEM","item":"LTB-001-time-check","source":"tutor_assessment"},"activeItem":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569523262-y5u5","source":"tutor"},"hintLevel":0,"qualityFlags":["learner_quote_mismatch"],"markerStatus":"ok"},"teaching":{"decisionId":"pd-5e91c680-b741-4a2f-b9a5-2c348fa34ce0","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-001","objectiveResolution":"lesson","primary":"formative_feedback","supporting":["retrieval_practice"],"modifiers":["adaptive_pathways","differentiated_instruction"],"reasonCodes":["NO_EVIDENCE"],"primaryVersion":1,"decisionVersion":"ped-v2","registryVersion":"reg-v2"},"attemptIds":["att-0005"],"attempts":1,"tutorAttempt":[{"id":"att-0005","status":200,"modelServed":"claude-opus-5-5","hasLtcBlock":true,"identifierLeaks":0,"systemSha256":"8a7a9d950647511a"}],"errorCode":null},{"turn":5,"learner":"After 12... so afternoon. But Good morning still ok, no? Morning is first, afternoon is second, so morning is more general?","runtimeParity":{"target":"simulated","tutorSawTarget":true,"acceptedAnswersInSystemPrompt":[],"activeItemBefore":{"id":"msg:msg-1794569523262-y5u5","source":"tutor"},"keyVerdict":null,"presentedLessonItemId":null,"markerStatus":"ok","markerInVisibleReply":false},"httpStatus":200,"latencyMs":8843,"reply":"Yes, 3 p.m. is **after** 12 p.m., so **afternoon** is right.\n\nYour idea \"morning is more general\" makes sense, but English doesn't work that way. The three time greetings are equal. Each one has its own time. None of them covers the whole day.\n\nThe **general** greeting is **\"Hello.\"** It works at any time.\n\nCompare:\n- 10 a.m.: \"Hello!\" ✓ \"Good morning!\" ✓\n- 4 p.m.: \"Hello!\" ✓ \"Good morning!\" ✗\n\nSo at 3 p.m., \"Good morning\" sounds wrong to English speakers.\n\n**Your task:** It's 8 p.m. You meet a new neighbour. Write a greeting with the time of day, and your name.","transport":"json","replyVersion":"enara-ai","languageTurn":{"version":"ltc-v1","lessonId":"ltb-lsn-001","objectiveId":"ltb-obj-001","skill":"written_interaction","moves":["reteach_simpler","comprehensible_model","comprehension_check"],"reasonCodes":["repeated_misconception_strategy_shift","level_beginner","during_feedback","after_explanation"],"supportRequested":false,"confusionSignals":0,"answeringCheck":true,"proficiency":{"status":"inferred","value":"A2","source":"course_level"},"nextStep":"reteac